  "workspaceId": "51a0788c-dc9c-4988-b43d-590d3d91bf8b",
  "dataSourceInstructions": "Use this semantic model for all tenant-specific Microsoft 365 license answers.\r\n\r\nUse existing measures instead of raw aggregations. Latest-snapshot measures already apply the newest snapshot; do not add another snapshot filter unless the user explicitly asks for history.\r\n\r\nInventory and assignments:\r\n- Use 'License SKU'[License Name] for normal product names. Use [SKU Part Number] only when the user asks for the API or admin-center SKU code.\r\n- Use [# Purchased Seats], [# Inventory Assigned Seats], and [# Available Seats] for subscription inventory.\r\n- Use [# Direct Assignments] and [# Group Assignments] for assignment source.\r\n- Microsoft Teams Premium is an add-on and Microsoft Teams Enterprise is a base license. Never treat them as substitutes.\r\n\r\nCost and pricing:\r\n- Costs are monthly Japanese yen. Format them with the yen sign and thousands separators.\r\n- [Monthly Cost] uses the configured unit price for every assigned seat.\r\n- Check 'SKU Price'[Price Source] before describing a cost as contractual. Public-list-price costs are estimates.\r\n\r\nOrganization and users:\r\n- Use 'User'[Department], [Office Location], [Company], [Country], [City], [Division], or [Cost Center] for breakdowns.\r\n- Missing organization values are stored as Unassigned.\r\n- For one-row-per-user answers, use the [利用状態] and [最終利用日] measures rather than raw utilization columns.\r\n\r\nE5 capabilities and service plans:\r\n- Use 'Service Plan'[機能名] as the business-friendly capability name and [サービスプラン品番] as the raw Microsoft Graph/admin-center plan code.\r\n- One capability can map to multiple service-plan codes. Preserve that hierarchy when the user asks for mapping details.\r\n- [有効ユーザー数] and [無効ユーザー数] describe license configuration derived from assignedLicenses.disabledPlans.\r\n- [機能の設定] returns 有効 only when all internal plans that compose the selected capability are enabled for that user; one disabled internal plan makes it 無効.\r\n- Enabled does not mean used. [利用中ユーザー数] counts enabled users who had any supported Microsoft 365 activity within 30 days; it is not feature-specific usage evidence. State this limitation whenever discussing capability usage.\r\n\r\nUtilization and Copilot:\r\n- Active means activity within 30 days, LowUsage means 31-89 days, Dormant means 90+ days, NeverUsed means no activity record, and DisabledAccount means sign-in blocked.\r\n- A Copilot prompt count of 0 is a measured zero, not missing data.\r\n\r\nAnswer only what was asked. Do not invent policy coverage, security telemetry, feature-specific usage, or license removal/downgrade recommendations. Answer in the language of the question and identify data limitations when they affect the conclusion.",
  "displayName": "M365 License FinOps Model",
  "type": "semantic_model",
  "userDescription": "Microsoft 365 license inventory, assignments, usage, cost, price source, and E5 capability configuration.",
